// @run
// @log 2
// THE WITNESS FOR A RETRACTED ARENA RUNG — check-clean INVALID WASM that no channel on
// this branch could see.
//
// `paramStructIndex` briefly asked the ARENA first
// (`structIndexOfTy(nodeTyIxOf(p.parType))`, falling back to `structIndexByName`). The
// dual-run that licensed it read 15,922 corpus calls with 41 disagreements, all one
// benign twin class, and 294 answers with 0 disagreements on the compiler's own source.
//
// It was blind. No corpus file declares a type whose name a FuncDecl type PARAMETER also
// uses — so no corpus file could disagree for the reason that matters. Here the shadow
// ruling says the parameter binds NOTHING and the real `T` wins, so the NAME's answer is
// correct; the arena's recorded type for a generic ORIGINAL's param is the UN-SUBSTITUTED
// shape, which is not that struct. The rung fronted the find and won with the wrong row:
// `vl check --codegen` rc 0, `vl run` "expected (ref null $type), found (ref $type)".
//
// Master ran this correctly throughout; only the branch broke it. Kept as a `@run` rather
// than an `@error` because the correct behaviour is that it WORKS — the nullable struct
// element is a `(ref null $T)` niche and `.length` is 2.
type T = { x: i32 }

function f<T>(v: { g: (T | null)[] }) {
  v.g.length
}

print(f({ g: [{ x: 1 }, null] }))
